00:00:15.820 --> 00:00:18.270
- Hi I'm Gena, I'm here with Ncuti Gatwa

00:00:18.270 --> 00:00:21.920
from "Sex Education" and
here are his Netflix Nine.

00:00:21.920 --> 00:00:23.100
I must say before we start,

00:00:23.100 --> 00:00:25.020
I'm so happy to have you here

00:00:25.020 --> 00:00:26.350
because I have been waiting

00:00:26.350 --> 00:00:27.393
for so long
- Aww!

00:00:28.630 --> 00:00:29.620
to get to speak to you.

00:00:29.620 --> 00:00:30.703
(laughing)

00:00:30.703 --> 00:00:31.536
I think you're great.

00:00:31.536 --> 00:00:33.190
I love Eric as a character.

00:00:33.190 --> 00:00:34.600
- Welcome to the Netflix Nine.

00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:35.569
- Thank you for having me.

00:00:35.569 --> 00:00:36.402
- Are you ready for the questions?

00:00:36.402 --> 00:00:37.300
- I am.

00:00:37.300 --> 00:00:39.200
- So my first question is about being

00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:40.770
on set in general with "Sex Education".

00:00:40.770 --> 00:00:42.340
Obviously, we're on the set today.

00:00:42.340 --> 00:00:44.150
Quite a big cast, it
appears as if you're all

00:00:44.150 --> 00:00:45.870
quite good friends from
Instagram, social media,

00:00:45.870 --> 00:00:47.000
schmah, schmah.

00:00:47.890 --> 00:00:49.840
Who makes you laugh the most on set,

00:00:49.840 --> 00:00:51.757
or makes it hardest for
you when you're filming?

00:00:51.757 --> 00:00:54.630
- Oh, easy, Aimee Lou Wood is a demon.

00:00:54.630 --> 00:00:58.940
There's no way you can be
in Aimee Lou Wood's company

00:00:58.940 --> 00:01:01.300
and not be like crying with laughter.

00:01:01.300 --> 00:01:02.133
- [Gena] Really?

00:01:02.133 --> 00:01:02.966
- Yeah.

00:01:02.966 --> 00:01:04.879
If you're in a scene with her, good luck.

00:01:04.879 --> 00:01:05.712
(laughs)

00:01:05.712 --> 00:01:08.193
Good luck to you, because
you'll be crying with laughter.

00:01:08.193 --> 00:01:09.412
- You grew up in Scotland,

00:01:09.412 --> 00:01:10.245
correct?
- Mm.

00:01:10.245 --> 00:01:11.410
So when you're away from home,

00:01:11.410 --> 00:01:14.200
what do you miss the most
about Scotland and the culture?

00:01:14.200 --> 00:01:15.486
- Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:01:15.486 --> 00:01:17.329
You've been doing your research!

00:01:17.329 --> 00:01:18.482
Look at you.

00:01:18.482 --> 00:01:19.918
- I'm not just any interviewer.

00:01:19.918 --> 00:01:21.734
- Okay, okay, then Gena.

00:01:21.734 --> 00:01:23.674
Big man tings and everything.

00:01:23.674 --> 00:01:27.560
So I'm, yeah, what do I
miss most about Scotland?

00:01:27.560 --> 00:01:28.435
The people.

00:01:28.435 --> 00:01:30.210
I miss the people, I think, like,

00:01:30.210 --> 00:01:32.000
when I first moved down to London,

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:33.330
people must have thought I was mad,

00:01:33.330 --> 00:01:34.560
'cause like where I'm from, like,

00:01:34.560 --> 00:01:36.750
you pass people in the
street and you say morning,

00:01:36.750 --> 00:01:38.090
even if you don't know them.

00:01:38.090 --> 00:01:42.324
And then, that is not something
that happens in London.

00:01:42.324 --> 00:01:43.175
- At all.

00:01:43.175 --> 00:01:44.008
- At all!

00:01:44.008 --> 00:01:45.059
- [Gena] Why are you doing that?

00:01:45.059 --> 00:01:46.195
Stop talking to me.
- Yeah.

00:01:46.195 --> 00:01:47.590
- People were looking at
me like, um, excuse me,

00:01:47.590 --> 00:01:48.670
like, why you trying to kill me?

00:01:48.670 --> 00:01:50.134
I think I miss, the kind of,

00:01:50.134 --> 00:01:51.420
(laughs)

00:01:51.420 --> 00:01:53.952
the manners, the manners and the warmth.

00:01:53.952 --> 00:01:55.710
- Londoners are a mannerless people.

00:01:55.710 --> 00:01:57.820
- I was gonna, yeah not really.

00:01:57.820 --> 00:02:00.240
People don't queue for the bus, in London,

00:02:00.240 --> 00:02:02.740
so it will just be like a free for all,

00:02:02.740 --> 00:02:04.837
like grannies getting
elbowed outta the way.

00:02:04.837 --> 00:02:06.974
- Grannies are the worst,
they'll be going in there.

00:02:06.974 --> 00:02:08.262
- Grannies are the worst!

00:02:08.262 --> 00:02:10.670
And they'll be hitting
you, like oh my God.

00:02:10.670 --> 00:02:13.796
But Londoners have a vibe that
you can't get anywhere else.

00:02:13.796 --> 00:02:16.663
- What's been your favorite
thing about being in Wales,

00:02:16.663 --> 00:02:18.970
your experience of filming
here and things like that?

00:02:18.970 --> 00:02:22.270
- Yeah, I think probably
just how beautiful it is.

00:02:22.270 --> 00:02:23.510
- It is stunning.

00:02:23.510 --> 00:02:25.700
It is so, so, so nice.

00:02:25.700 --> 00:02:27.000
As I was driving here I was like, "What?"

00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:29.360
- Yeah, it literally is like,

00:02:29.360 --> 00:02:31.730
sometimes you're like
is this the real world?

00:02:31.730 --> 00:02:34.300
Like is this in the UK?

00:02:34.300 --> 00:02:35.133
- Yes!

00:02:35.133 --> 00:02:39.330
- I did not think the UK
could hold such beauty.

00:02:39.330 --> 00:02:41.240
The friendliness of Welsh people,

00:02:41.240 --> 00:02:43.099
just the banter of Welsh people.

00:02:43.099 --> 00:02:46.090
I'd say like Cardiff is
also really multi-cultural,

00:02:46.090 --> 00:02:47.247
I was saying to you before,

00:02:47.247 --> 00:02:48.680
like it's really, really,
really multi-cultural

00:02:48.680 --> 00:02:51.060
and like, people are just
really friendly here.

00:02:51.060 --> 00:02:53.260
- Okay, so in my opinion you already have

00:02:53.260 --> 00:02:55.720
a personality that is
literally made for fame.

00:02:55.720 --> 00:02:57.033
You're so hilarious.
- Aw.

00:02:57.033 --> 00:02:58.920
But for you, what's it been like

00:02:58.920 --> 00:03:00.470
to be propelled into fame this way?

00:03:00.470 --> 00:03:02.067
How often do you get spotted?

00:03:02.067 --> 00:03:03.139
What're you saying?

00:03:03.139 --> 00:03:08.139
- Yeah, spotted, it's
definitely a daily occurrence.

00:03:08.790 --> 00:03:10.080
It's definitely a daily occurrence.

00:03:10.080 --> 00:03:11.370
Can't go to Tesco anymore.

00:03:11.370 --> 00:03:13.219
(laughs)

00:03:13.219 --> 00:03:15.043
No, I do, I definitely do.

00:03:16.270 --> 00:03:17.660
Yeah, it's odd.

00:03:17.660 --> 00:03:22.626
I was in America with
Emma and Asa doing press

00:03:22.626 --> 00:03:24.510
the day that the show was released.

00:03:24.510 --> 00:03:28.328
So, I hopped on the plane
coming back to the UK

00:03:28.328 --> 00:03:30.156
with like my 500 followers.

00:03:30.156 --> 00:03:35.156
Eight hours later, woke up
on the plane to like 700,000.

00:03:35.580 --> 00:03:36.879
And I was like, yeah.

00:03:36.879 --> 00:03:37.712
- [Gina] 700,000?

00:03:37.712 --> 00:03:40.160
- 700,000, like a small country.

00:03:40.160 --> 00:03:41.710
I was like, "Whoa!"

00:03:41.710 --> 00:03:42.543
- That's actually wild!

00:03:42.543 --> 00:03:43.523
- Hey!

00:03:43.523 --> 00:03:44.701
Can you imagine?

00:03:44.701 --> 00:03:45.784
I was like...

00:03:46.633 --> 00:03:47.466
- Oh my God.

00:03:47.466 --> 00:03:48.730
- What is going on, yeah.

00:03:48.730 --> 00:03:50.270
My phone was just like,
- Wow!

00:03:50.270 --> 00:03:53.420
like just going crazy out of control.

00:03:53.420 --> 00:03:57.570
So, that was odd, and then
like people recognized me.

00:03:57.570 --> 00:04:00.010
Bruv, it's so weird having
people recognize you.

00:04:00.010 --> 00:04:00.843
- Yeah.

00:04:00.843 --> 00:04:03.260
- And also, I live in Tottenham,
like I live in the ends.

00:04:03.260 --> 00:04:06.410
So like if someone just
grabs your arm in the street

00:04:06.410 --> 00:04:08.300
or if someone just
comes up into your face,

00:04:08.300 --> 00:04:09.160
you might get a slap.

00:04:09.160 --> 00:04:10.020
- Yeah, exactly.

00:04:10.020 --> 00:04:11.370
- I might slap you.

00:04:11.370 --> 00:04:12.473
What are you doing there?
(Gena laughs)

00:04:12.473 --> 00:04:13.440
What are you doing?

00:04:13.440 --> 00:04:14.700
- So like a few times when
you're in Oxford Street

00:04:14.700 --> 00:04:18.520
and someone grabs your arm,
it's like I'm like ready,

00:04:18.520 --> 00:04:20.494
I'm ready, and then they're
like "Oh, my God I love you".

00:04:20.494 --> 00:04:23.310
And then it's like oh
okay, this is so odd.

00:04:23.310 --> 00:04:25.150
I don't know how to take this.

00:04:25.150 --> 00:04:28.057
- So, other than yourself,
who is your favorite,

00:04:28.057 --> 00:04:29.250
I'm not saying that you think you're

00:04:29.250 --> 00:04:30.812
your favorite character but you're mine.

00:04:30.812 --> 00:04:31.645
- Aw!

00:04:31.645 --> 00:04:33.149
- So who's your favorite
character on "Sex Education"

00:04:33.149 --> 00:04:33.982
and why?

00:04:33.982 --> 00:04:37.380
- Can't decide between
Jackson, Aimee and Maeve.

00:04:37.380 --> 00:04:40.960
I'd say probably between Aimee and Maeve,

00:04:40.960 --> 00:04:43.010
like I love Aimee's storylines.

00:04:43.010 --> 00:04:45.960
Like in season one I just
thought that was so great.

00:04:45.960 --> 00:04:48.142
Sex is something that's
been so like geared

00:04:48.142 --> 00:04:52.400
and manufactured towards male
pleasure and the male gaze,

00:04:52.400 --> 00:04:54.520
and I think that her
storyline really highlighted

00:04:54.520 --> 00:04:55.740
that it's not,

00:04:55.740 --> 00:04:58.703
and figure out whatever
the hell you wanna do.

00:04:59.880 --> 00:05:00.820
So that I really like.

00:05:00.820 --> 00:05:03.331
Her storyline this year is sick as well.

00:05:03.331 --> 00:05:05.210
But Maeve is just so bad-ass.

00:05:05.210 --> 00:05:06.043
It's quite empowering.

00:05:06.043 --> 00:05:08.700
Even Emma as a person,
whenever I stand beside her

00:05:08.700 --> 00:05:10.500
I'm like who's gonna touch me?

00:05:10.500 --> 00:05:11.720
Which one of you lot are gonna touch me?

00:05:11.720 --> 00:05:12.913
None of you lot can touch me,

00:05:12.913 --> 00:05:13.746
I'm with my muckie.
- I'm with my girl.

00:05:13.746 --> 00:05:16.270
Yeah yeah yeah, I'm
with my girl right now.

00:05:16.270 --> 00:05:18.210
So yeah, probably those two.

00:05:18.210 --> 00:05:20.624
And Jackson, I mean Kedar's my boy.

00:05:20.624 --> 00:05:21.457
- [Gina] Yeah?

00:05:21.457 --> 00:05:22.850
- And Jackson, I just think having

00:05:22.850 --> 00:05:27.726
a dark-skinned boy go through
depression and anxiety

00:05:27.726 --> 00:05:31.530
and all these things
and pressure to achieve.

00:05:31.530 --> 00:05:33.030
These are issues that we face,

00:05:33.030 --> 00:05:35.190
you know, and they never get discussed.

00:05:35.190 --> 00:05:39.020
And so I just rate his representation.

00:05:39.020 --> 00:05:40.070
- I agree.

00:05:40.070 --> 00:05:41.160
Fantastic answer.

00:05:41.160 --> 00:05:43.390
You came through with the male gaze, okay.

00:05:43.390 --> 00:05:44.223
- Thank you.

00:05:44.223 --> 00:05:45.977
Come on, you know, I've got a degree.

00:05:45.977 --> 00:05:47.020
(laughs)

00:05:47.020 --> 00:05:49.270
- So you are a celebrity in my eyes,

00:05:49.270 --> 00:05:50.460
just accepting it.

00:05:50.460 --> 00:05:52.300
If I say it then...

00:05:52.300 --> 00:05:53.133
- It's fact.

00:05:53.133 --> 00:05:54.073
(laughs)

00:05:54.073 --> 00:05:56.950
- So, since you're a celebrity,
if you could swap lives

00:05:56.950 --> 00:06:00.550
with any other celebrity, who would it be?

00:06:00.550 --> 00:06:01.690
I'll give you another option,

00:06:01.690 --> 00:06:03.550
you could also choose to
be best friends with one.

00:06:03.550 --> 00:06:04.578
- Okay!

00:06:04.578 --> 00:06:06.230
- So, swap lives, or best
friends with a celebrity.

00:06:06.230 --> 00:06:07.530
- Okay, now we're talking.

00:06:08.852 --> 00:06:11.435
(upbeat music)

00:06:12.290 --> 00:06:15.370
- I mean, it has to be Rihanna, hasn't it?

00:06:15.370 --> 00:06:17.560
- Ooh, that's a good choice.

00:06:17.560 --> 00:06:20.460
- It has to be Rihanna for
both of those questions.

00:06:20.460 --> 00:06:23.010
I would want to be her.

00:06:23.010 --> 00:06:25.740
I mean who wouldn't want to live that?

00:06:25.740 --> 00:06:26.640
Come on!

00:06:26.640 --> 00:06:30.215
And to be best friends
with Rihanna, my God!

00:06:30.215 --> 00:06:31.300
That would be cool.

00:06:31.300 --> 00:06:32.200
- She would look after you.

00:06:32.200 --> 00:06:34.500
- She would look after
you, you'd have fun.

00:06:34.500 --> 00:06:35.333
- [Gena] You would.

00:06:35.333 --> 00:06:40.010
- But you'd also be part
of changing culture,

00:06:40.010 --> 00:06:42.550
I mean that Fenty
Beauty, what she dropped,

00:06:42.550 --> 00:06:43.690
like changed the game.

00:06:43.690 --> 00:06:47.140
I want to witness that
alongside my best friends.

00:06:47.140 --> 00:06:48.277
Rihanna, yeah.

00:06:48.277 --> 00:06:50.262
But I'm happy for you, RiRi.

00:06:50.262 --> 00:06:51.300
- Love you girl.

00:06:51.300 --> 00:06:52.820
- I love you girl, I'm proud of you.

00:06:52.820 --> 00:06:54.310
Yeah!

00:06:54.310 --> 00:06:55.908
- A large part of Eric's storyline

00:06:55.908 --> 00:06:57.678
is his relationship with his dad.

00:06:57.678 --> 00:07:00.380
How that progresses and then
it culminates, obviously,

00:07:00.380 --> 00:07:02.540
in, I think it's episode
seven, from the prom.

00:07:02.540 --> 00:07:04.600
It was such a lovely moment.

00:07:04.600 --> 00:07:07.343
- I want you to be proud and strong.

00:07:08.740 --> 00:07:10.460
But you are so different.

00:07:11.992 --> 00:07:14.320
It makes me feel scared for you.

00:07:14.320 --> 00:07:17.510
- What was it like working
with your on-screen dad

00:07:17.510 --> 00:07:19.580
and how did you get into
that space emotionally?

00:07:19.580 --> 00:07:21.980
- It was so great working with Deobia.

00:07:21.980 --> 00:07:25.830
He's an amazing actor and
he brings a lot of weight

00:07:25.830 --> 00:07:30.130
and a lot of truth and
intention to whatever he does.

00:07:30.130 --> 00:07:33.226
And it was just great to be around that,

00:07:33.226 --> 00:07:35.912
like an actor who takes
it really seriously.

00:07:35.912 --> 00:07:39.400
And offers quite a lot, more
than what's on the page.

00:07:39.400 --> 00:07:42.540
'Cause that's what I try to do,

00:07:42.540 --> 00:07:45.340
is like lift things off the page

00:07:45.340 --> 00:07:46.173
and he's really good at that

00:07:46.173 --> 00:07:48.833
and so it was great being around him.

00:07:49.770 --> 00:07:54.330
You know what, just
like as two black actors

00:07:54.330 --> 00:07:56.800
we have a shared experience in life

00:07:56.800 --> 00:07:59.183
and so it was really
great to tap into that,

00:07:59.183 --> 00:08:02.085
into the fact that we kind of just get it.

00:08:02.085 --> 00:08:04.340
We get what the culture is.

00:08:04.340 --> 00:08:06.526
We understood, do you know what I mean?

00:08:06.526 --> 00:08:10.020
Quite a lot of it was us talking about it.

00:08:10.020 --> 00:08:12.300
Shout out to Netflix and
shout out to the writers

00:08:12.300 --> 00:08:13.540
and to everyone at "Sex Education"

00:08:13.540 --> 00:08:16.650
because they're really
great at collaborating,

00:08:16.650 --> 00:08:19.097
and quite often the
writers will ask me like,

00:08:19.097 --> 00:08:21.183
"Is this right about this church scene?"

00:08:21.183 --> 00:08:23.510
Stuff like that so they're really invested

00:08:23.510 --> 00:08:26.290
in making things right
and gave us the freedom

00:08:26.290 --> 00:08:27.870
to kind of like talk to each other

00:08:27.870 --> 00:08:29.710
and see what works for us.

00:08:29.710 --> 00:08:31.359
And so that was very helpful.

00:08:31.359 --> 00:08:32.530
- I love that.

00:08:32.530 --> 00:08:35.287
Speaking of bringing
characters off the page.

00:08:35.287 --> 00:08:36.350
(laughs)

00:08:36.350 --> 00:08:37.183
- Yeah, oh my God.

00:08:37.183 --> 00:08:38.016
What is this now?

00:08:38.016 --> 00:08:39.040
Gena?

00:08:39.040 --> 00:08:40.138
(laughing)

00:08:40.138 --> 00:08:42.340
Gena what have you got planned?

00:08:42.340 --> 00:08:44.450
- Imagine if I was like...

00:08:44.450 --> 00:08:46.661
When I first watched Sex Education,

00:08:46.661 --> 00:08:50.331
what struck me about your
character were the little

00:08:50.331 --> 00:08:52.888
like punctuations in speech
and things like that.

00:08:52.888 --> 00:08:55.650
But there's a scene where Eric and Otis

00:08:55.650 --> 00:08:57.125
are walking down the bridge.

00:08:57.125 --> 00:08:58.910
(laughs)

00:08:58.910 --> 00:09:00.067
- Like, you're a hidiot.

00:09:00.067 --> 00:09:01.210
- [Eric] Look at you laughing...

00:09:01.210 --> 00:09:02.043
- [Otis] It's not funny.

00:09:02.043 --> 00:09:02.876
- [Eric] Like a dickhead.

00:09:02.876 --> 00:09:03.709
- [Otis] Shut up.

00:09:03.709 --> 00:09:04.560
- [Eric] Like a fool.

00:09:04.560 --> 00:09:05.393
- [Otis] All right.

00:09:05.393 --> 00:09:06.226
- [Eric] Like a hidiot.

00:09:06.226 --> 00:09:07.499
- [Otis] Go clean yourself off.

00:09:07.499 --> 00:09:08.651
(laughing)

00:09:08.651 --> 00:09:09.890
- You were like, um, there's plenty more

00:09:09.890 --> 00:09:11.569
scary bad fish in-a the sea.

00:09:11.569 --> 00:09:12.978
- In-a the sea.

00:09:12.978 --> 00:09:13.811
- Who wrote that?

00:09:13.811 --> 00:09:15.364
It was so authentic though,

00:09:15.364 --> 00:09:17.907
this is why I already felt
like I was friends with you.

00:09:17.907 --> 00:09:20.880
It was so real to my
experience with my friends

00:09:20.880 --> 00:09:22.210
and how we speak.

00:09:22.210 --> 00:09:23.990
How much of those sorts of things,

00:09:23.990 --> 00:09:26.100
those punctuations, little
things that Eric does,

00:09:26.100 --> 00:09:27.900
how much of that is improv from you?

00:09:27.900 --> 00:09:29.240
How much of that is written for you?

00:09:29.240 --> 00:09:31.380
How much of yourself did you bring to it?

00:09:31.380 --> 00:09:36.380
